# What must not travel to the build.
#
# `az acr build` uploads the whole context before anything is built, so what is
# listed here is the difference between a fast build and one that sends hundreds
# of megabytes of dependencies to be discarded on arrival.
#
# The image installs its own dependencies from the lockfiles. Anything already
# installed here is for a different operating system anyway.

**/node_modules/
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/dist/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# History, not source.
.git/
.github/

# Local run state and its logs.
.run/

# Test artefacts.
web/cypress/videos/
web/cypress/screenshots/
web/cypress/downloads/
coverage/

# Secrets, and the file naming what a previous provision created.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/azure/environment.json

# The deployment's own definitions. The image is built from a Dockerfile that
# is passed in by path; it does not need to contain its siblings.
deploy/
